WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
SPEAKER: You can find just
about anything on the internet.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.530
But when you click
a link, how do you

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.150
know what's on the other side?

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.250
Phishing and malware are
more prevalent than ever

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.380
and pose a real threat to
the personal information

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.480
of yourself and your users.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.570
You can make sure your users
can quickly identify bad sites

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.730
and help protect their
information with Web

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.350
Risk from Google Cloud.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.330
Web Risk contains a
fully managed database

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.310
of URL threats that
you can scan against

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.110
to know if the URL is safe.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.110
Once if it's unsafe, you
can take appropriate action,

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.510
such as blocking the content
or letting your users know

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.920
they shouldn't proceed.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.050
When you look up a
URL, Google checks

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.810
to see if it's in the
database of known unsafe URLs.

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.510
This database is constantly
updated by scanning over

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.940
1 billion URLs every day.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.460
Using a combination of
rules, machine learning,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.310
and human analysis, URLs
are gathered and scanned

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.110
from sources like Google Search.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.570
The Web Risk database is
constantly kept up to date,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.190
so you and your users
can be confident

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.690
that the analysis is
reliable and accurate.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.140
So the next time user
generated content is posted,

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.730
your users can
feel secure knowing

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.030
that you've protected them
against any malicious URLs.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.850
Getting started with the
Web Risk Lookup API is easy.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.370
Once you've enabled the
API, all you need to do

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.070
is submit the URL to be checked
against Google's block list.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.720
If there's no result,
the URL is safe.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.780
Otherwise, Google will
return what type of threat

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.700
has been detected
and when you'll

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.210
want to call the API again to
check if it's still unsafe.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.800
To get started
with a Lookup API,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.180
we'll head over to the console.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.070
From the search at the
top, search for Web

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.260
Risk so that we can
enable the API for use

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.590
in this Google Cloud project.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.180
Now we can create
a service account

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.020
to securely call the API, so
click Credentials and then

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.393
Create Credentials.

00:01:38.393 --> 00:01:40.560
We'll make a service account
called Web Risk Runner.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.720
Once that's created, we can
download the service account

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.810
key to easily make API calls on
behalf of our service account.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.690
Now we can switch
to Cloud Shell,

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.160
or you can use a
local environment

00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.170
with G Cloud already set up.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.210
First, we can set the
application credentials

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.890
to point to the
service account key.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.200
Then, all we need to
do is run this command.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.080
This command makes a
request to the Web Risk

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.340
API using our service
account credentials.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.138
Here, we're looking for malware
on the URL testsafebrowsing

00:02:15.138 --> 00:02:21.990
.appspot.com/s/malware.html,
and the response confirms that

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:25.080
malware has been detected on
the URL as well as an expiration

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.660
time so that we could cache the
result locally and know when

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.510
to scan this particular URL.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:32.310
There's more than
just the Lookup API.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.900
If you're looking
for lower latency

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.700
or for private
scanning, Web Risk

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.880
also offers an offline database
through the Update API.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.880
For even more details, you
can use the Evaluation API

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.430
to get a confidence score
and the Submission API

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.100
to report suspected URLs.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.380
There's a lot of URLs
out there, so get

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.295
started for free with Web Risk
today to protect your users.

00:02:52.295 --> 00:02:53.670
Check out the link
to learn more.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.020
[MUSIC PLAYING]

